    <chapter title="Custom transformers" id="custom_transformers">
        <p>
            A transformer converts a supported value before the converter serializes it. Register transformer class
            names in <path>config/feeds.php</path>. Laravel resolves each class through the service container, so
            constructor dependencies and custom container bindings are supported.
        </p>

        <code-block lang="php" src="advanced-extends-transformer.php" include-lines="5-" />

        <p>
            Add the transformer to the configured list after the built-in transformers:
        </p>

        <code-block lang="php" src="advanced-extends-transformer-config.php" />

        <p>
            The configured transformers run in declaration order. Each <code>allow()</code> call receives the current
            value, including changes made by earlier transformers, and every matching transformer may update it.
            Duplicate entries are removed after container resolution while the first occurrence keeps its position.
        </p>

        <p>
            A converter builds this ordered pipeline once and reuses the same transformer instances for every field
            in that feed generation.
        </p>

        <chapter title="Feed-local transformers" id="feed_local_transformers">
            <p>
                Override <code>transformers()</code> on a feed to apply transformers only to that feed. The method
                returns transformer class names, and Laravel resolves them through the service container in the same
                way as the global list.
            </p>

            <p>
                For example, define a date transformer with a feed-specific format:
            </p>

            <code-block lang="php" src="advanced-extends-transformer-local.php" include-lines="5-" />

            <p>
                Then return it from the feed:
            </p>

            <code-block lang="php" src="advanced-extends-transformer-feed.php" include-lines="5-" />

            <p>
                The local list does not replace the global list from <path>config/feeds.php</path>. Transformers run in
                this order:
            </p>

            <list type="decimal">
                <li>Feed-local transformers returned by <code>transformers()</code>.</li>
                <li>Global transformers from <path>config/feeds.php</path>.</li>
                <li>Converter-specific transformers required by the selected output format.</li>
            </list>

            <p>
                A local transformer can therefore format a date first. The global date transformer receives the
                resulting string and skips it, while other global transformers still process matching fields.
            </p>
        </chapter>
    </chapter>
